  "verbalization": "Tiapride is shown to have targets in the pathways of Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 2 and Valacyclovir hydrolase, both of which are implicated in the targeting of HaCaT cells. The evidence suggests that Tiapride may exert its effects on HaCaT through the modulation of these enzymes, which are involved in cellular metabolism and possibly contribute to the observed biological activity. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism by which Tiapride interacts with HaCaT, possibly through the inhibition of metabolic pathways that are critical for cell survival or function. The presence of multiple targets, each with a direct link to HaCaT, supports a role for Tiapride in modulating cellular processes in this cell line, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
